# Documentation Index

This directory contains supporting documentation for the AutoSUT artifact.

## Start Here

- `../README.md`: top-level repository overview
- `../REVIEWER_GUIDE.md`: canonical validation workflow
- `../REPRODUCIBILITY.md`: reproducibility scope and limits
- `../ARCHITECTURE.md`: layered architecture summary
- `../PUBLIC_REPOSITORY_SCOPE.md`: publication boundaries for GitHub and artifact distribution

## Supporting Documents

- `reviewer_quickstart.md`: shortest evaluator path and optional live replay
- `reproducibility.md`: detailed notes aligned with the host-only claim gate
  and optional Docker replay
- `architecture.md`: expanded architecture discussion
- `architecture/EXECUTION_MODEL.md`: released paths versus optional backend
  implementation material
- `SEMANTIC_ENRICHMENT_PROTOCOL.md`: Step-2 proposal and provenance boundary
- `WINDOWS_PROVIDER_DEVELOPMENT.md`: native-Windows development and promotion
  rule
- `NATIVE_WINDOWS_CORPUS_ADJUDICATION.md`: human-adjudication protocol for
  deciding whether native Windows is scientifically required

## Notes

- Reviewer-facing claims should be grounded in the top-level documents first:
  `README.md`, `REVIEWER_GUIDE.md`, `REPRODUCIBILITY.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`,
  and `PUBLIC_REPOSITORY_SCOPE.md`.
- Historical operational notes, browser-triggered run services, and predecessor
  documentation are intentionally excluded from the public package.
